# Discovering Hidden Analogies in an Online Humanities Database.

**Authors:** Cory, Kenneth A.

## Abstract
Contends that large databases contain hidden knowledge, or literature that is logically linked but not bibliographically linked, that contains academically interesting commonalities not retrievable by normal searching methods. Based on search methods for discovering previously unknown causes of medical syndromes, a method for discovering new humanities analogies is constructed and tested. (DSK)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ580634

